Subject: [PATCH] sprd: complete stock camera sequencing and unwind failed GPU starts

Follow-up to CharlesGool/e5-sleep-kernel e5-sleep2 patches 0004/0005.
Camera sequence verified against E5 stock qogirn6l operations (Android 13):
sprd_cam_pw_on.58 0x25b4, sprd_cam_pw_off.59 0x2d80. Keep DT register/mask
selection, propagate bus failures, check three stable PMU reads and gate the
clock only after confirmed shutdown. Built-in provider owns its lifetime.
Do not change suspend policy, radio operation, polling or eMMC sleep.

--- a/drivers/soc/sprd/domain/sprd_camsys_pd.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sprd/domain/sprd_camsys_pd.c
@@ -1,22 +1,11 @@
-// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 /*
- * Camera subsystem power domain for UMS9621 ("qogirn6lite").
- *
- * The camera block (PD_CAMERA in the PMU) has no auto shutdown and comes out
- * of the bootloader powered, with its AON MM_EB gate open.  The stock kernel's
- * camera driver forces it off whenever no camera is open; without that the
- * AP subsystem never enters PMU deep sleep during system suspend
- * (AP_DEEP_SLEEP_CNT stays at 0).  This driver turns the vendor node
- * ("sprd,qogirl6l-camsys-domain", <&mm_domain>) into a generic PM domain
- * that starts off, so the domain is powered only while a consumer (ISP, DCAM,
- * JPEG, a sensor) is runtime active -- which on these boards is never.
- *
- * The register layout comes from the vendor DT as <&syscon reg mask>
- * triples, the same way the vendor driver reads it.
- *
- * Copyright (C) 2026 The e5-linux project
+ * UMS9621 camera power domain. Based on CharlesGool/e5-sleep-kernel
+ * e5-sleep2 (52ad641), with the DCAM/ISP/top sequence verified against
+ * E5's stock sprd_camsys_pw_domain.ko, qogirn6l operations.
+ * Registers and masks come from the original device tree.
  */
